{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082167-augment-mind-limit-to-reach-mana-turn-and-spells-with-crossover-in-mind","id":1082167,"title":"Augment Mind, Limit to Reach & Mana/Turn, and Spells with Crossover in mind","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-22T00:08:42-07:00","id":1082167,"title":"Augment Mind, Limit to Reach & Mana/Turn, and Spells with Crossover in mind","content":"Big title - lots of little questions: I'm new to Mage, and there are some details that I need some assistance on that I may have missed in the books so clarification would nice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> :<br /> <br /> So question - with Augment Mind spell for example:<br /> <br /> The mage is capable of increasing the subject\u2019s mental or<br /> social capacity. The mage can increase one of either the subject\u2019s<br /> Mental or Social Attributes by one dot per level of Potency of<br /> the spell. This increase affects any Advantages or other traits<br /> derived from the Attribute\u2019s level. The spell cannot increase the<br /> subject\u2019s Attribute above her normal maximum allowed by her<br /> Gnosis. The benefits of this spell are not obvious to a casual<br /> observer, but those who know the subject may notice an increase<br /> in her intellect or charismatic nature.<br /> +1 Reach The mage may increase an additional Attribute with<br /> the spell for each additional Reach, dividing the spell\u2019s Potency<br /> among them. For example, the mage may spend +2 Reach with<br /> a Potency 4 spell and increase the subject\u2019s Intelligence by +1,<br /> Resolve by +2, and Wits by +1.<br /> + 2 Reach By spending a point of Mana, the mage my increase<br /> her subject\u2019s Mental or Social Attributes above the normal<br /> maximum allowed.<br /> <br /> My question is one in that I'm playing in a crossover setting. So with going beyond 2 reach for example: can the player basically give free attribute dots to players for a permanent duration? What are the penalties with doing so? Can the player just pass free attribute dots? And if so - with +2 reach - could the mage permanently give like.... +6 intelligence dots or even like +4 to go beyond the attribute limit (I know potency, and reach, are all factors)The campaign also has Kindred &amp; Unchained and making pacts with players. Could my Unchained make Pacts with the Mage for free attribute dots (like a pact of intelligence for an intelligence dot? ) - I'm fairly new to Mage and obviously I may be mistaken on things, so clarification is always nice. Thanks in advance and sorry for the confusing title <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T00:41:08-07:00","id":1082170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082167-augment-mind-limit-to-reach-mana-turn-and-spells-with-crossover-in-mind#post1082167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is one in that I'm playing in a crossover setting. So with going beyond 2 reach for example: can the player basically give free attribute dots to players for a permanent duration?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're in a setting without a lot of other/hostile mages, are prepared to invest Willpower dots in relinquishing spells for the long term or Reach a lot to cast other spells, and don't draw a distinction between &quot;permanent&quot; and &quot;until dispelled,&quot; sure.<br /> <br /> The non-mage PCs may find it a little troublesome when being long-term subjects of your spells and/or associates of you as a mage causes them to become affected by your Long-Term Nimbus \u2014 a demon has enough on her plate without also turning into a magnet for emotional disturbances, and few vampires would relish the prospect of potentially drawing a being of sunlight and cinder to their haven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T00:46:36-07:00","id":1082173,"title":"","content":"You increase subjects mental capacity by taking a -2 dice penalty on the casting roll for each dot you want to improve. You get a base potency equal to your mind arcanum -1. You also need to take a -2 penalty per duration step you want (and 1 reach to make it advanced duration). Note your only going to get 1 free reach unless you have this spell as a rote in which case you will have 3 free reaches and only incur paradox dice on the 4th reach.<br /> <br /> If you have mind 3 then your base spell has a potency of 3 for each -2 on the casting roll you get +1 potency spell factor. So for +6 (3 base + 3) intelligence you need to take a -6 penalty &amp; use +2 reach to go over max. You then need to spend another -10 penalty and another +1 reach for a indefinate duration (not permanent) advanced duration factor.<br /> <br /> Your base dicepool with gnosis 1 will be 4, you can add 1 yantra (say +2 from highspeech), additional +1 per ritual casting time to a max of 5 (instant requires another reach) and willpower for a total dicepool of 14 - 16 = -2 (you cant cast a spell if the penalties after bonus takes it lower than -5) so you have a chance die and the spell will take a base of 3 hours + 3x5 additional hours so 18 total hours to cast. If not cast as a rote your 2 reach over your free reaches, if a rote your ok for paradox (unless seen by sleepers etc).<br /> <br /> Also remember mages have a limited number of spells they can control and will probably need to relinquish them, but theres nothing stopping them from buffing the entire group either, they can take some reach more penalties and increase the number of targets. So the above spell could give 2 subjects +6 intelligence and be at a total dice pool of -4 which is still a chance dice but possible.<br /> <br /> Id need to read up on demon pacts but remember making pacts with mages is probably as dangerous as making pacts with a demon, fate can allow them to ignore, change and do nasty things to oaths etc.<br /> <br /> So theres nothing stopping a friendly mage buffing the group except spell control, paradox mitigation, willpower recovery for relinquished spells etc etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-22-2017, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T01:07:59-07:00","id":1082175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082167-augment-mind-limit-to-reach-mana-turn-and-spells-with-crossover-in-mind?p=1082170#post1082170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're in a setting without a lot of other/hostile mages, are prepared to invest Willpower dots in relinquishing spells for the long term or Reach a lot to cast other spells, and don't draw a distinction between &quot;permanent&quot; and &quot;until dispelled,&quot; sure.<br /> <br /> The non-mage PCs may find it a little troublesome when being long-term subjects of your spells and/or associates of you as a mage causes them to become affected by your Long-Term Nimbus \u2014 a demon has enough on her plate without also turning into a magnet for emotional disturbances, and few vampires would relish the prospect of potentially drawing a being of sunlight and cinder to their haven.</div> </div> </div> </div>So for clarification of this as the storyteller of the game, (player was asking about it, as I wondered if he could just give the party ridiculous permanent bonuses as he thought it was unfair so I figured I'd check), what do you mean about the willpower investment? Also does Reach/Mana per spell have a limit? And permanent &amp; Until Dispelled are different I assume in that permanent can't be dispelled - sorry Mage compared to all the other splats does my head in , the rules seem so complicated even after reading it so many times xD.<br /> <br /> Also - Thanks for the help ^-^ in advance<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T01:13:45-07:00","id":1082176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082167-augment-mind-limit-to-reach-mana-turn-and-spells-with-crossover-in-mind?p=1082173#post1082173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You increase subjects mental capacity by taking a -2 dice penalty on the casting roll for each dot you want to improve. You get a base potency equal to your mind arcanum -1. You also need to take a -2 penalty per duration step you want (and 1 reach to make it advanced duration). Note your only going to get 1 free reach unless you have this spell as a rote in which case you will have 3 free reaches and only incur paradox dice on the 4th reach.<br /> <br /> If you have mind 3 then your base spell has a potency of 3 for each -2 on the casting roll you get +1 potency spell factor. So for +6 (3 base + 3) intelligence you need to take a -6 penalty &amp; use +2 reach to go over max. You then need to spend another -10 penalty and another +1 reach for a indefinate duration (not permanent) advanced duration factor.<br /> <br /> Your base dicepool with gnosis 1 will be 4, you can add 1 yantra (say +2 from highspeech), additional +1 per ritual casting time to a max of 5 (instant requires another reach) and willpower for a total dicepool of 14 - 16 = -2 (you cant cast a spell if the penalties after bonus takes it lower than -5) so you have a chance die and the spell will take a base of 3 hours + 3x5 additional hours so 18 total hours to cast. If not cast as a rote your 2 reach over your free reaches, if a rote your ok for paradox (unless seen by sleepers etc).<br /> <br /> Also remember mages have a limited number of spells they can control and will probably need to relinquish them, but theres nothing stopping them from buffing the entire group either, they can take some reach more penalties and increase the number of targets. So the above spell could give 2 subjects +6 intelligence and be at a total dice pool of -4 which is still a chance dice but possible.<br /> <br /> Id need to read up on demon pacts but remember making pacts with mages is probably as dangerous as making pacts with a demon, fate can allow them to ignore, change and do nasty things to oaths etc.<br /> <br /> So theres nothing stopping a friendly mage buffing the group except spell control, paradox mitigation, willpower recovery for relinquished spells etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so indefinite is different from permanent in what way exactly? If it's dispelled? And so if that spell is considered *active* - where is the spell limit? <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Also - Thanks for the help ^-^ in advance, sorry for silly questions lol.</span><br /> </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T01:22:22-07:00","id":1082178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082167-augment-mind-limit-to-reach-mana-turn-and-spells-with-crossover-in-mind?p=1082176#post1082176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so indefinite is different from permanent in what way exactly? If it's dispelled? And so if that spell is considered *active* - where is the spell limit? <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Also - Thanks for the help ^-^ in advance, sorry for silly questions lol.</span></span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Spell limits or spell control is equal to the mages Gnosis rating. Indefinate spells stick around until dispelled or erased by dissonance or ended by the caster. Note that mages can cast additional spells over their spell control but each one requires additional reach which invites more paradox etc etc..<br /> <br /> Relinquishing spells &quot;safely&quot; requires spending a dot of willpower, which costs 1 exp to get back? Spells unsafely relinquished go awry and can end early<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;&gt; <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">At the beginning of<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">every chapter, the Storyteller rolls one die for every Reach the<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">spell used above the caster\u2019s free Reach, or a chance die if it was<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">within her limits. A dramatic failure means the spell skips the<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">roll for the next chapter; success grants the Storyteller a Reach<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">as though the spell had gained a Paradox; and an exceptional<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">success ends the spell, canceling its remaining Duration.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>There is no such thing as permanent spells, only the lasting effects caused by them.<br /> <br /> Still not 100% sure what you were asking to be honest. I think the answer is yes mages can give stats to people but its not as easy as people claim, theres no limit to reaching except one gets more paradox dice (which has various ways to mitigate) and mages can spend a certain amount of mana per turn but during ritual casting there is no maxium, as for pacts with mages im not sure i have only skimmed demon.<br /> <br /> Forgot to add the +1 mana cost for advanced duration above too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-22-2017, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T01:40:28-07:00","id":1082179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082167-augment-mind-limit-to-reach-mana-turn-and-spells-with-crossover-in-mind?p=1082175#post1082175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what do you mean about the willpower investment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Making a spell not count towards your Gnosis limit of controlled spells without causing the effect to degrade over time requires that the caster spend a Willpower dot, which costs experience to repurchase. Until then, that spell counts toward your spell control and effectively reduces the number of spells you can have active at the same time by one until you end the spell, which makes it harder to cast other spells without risking Paradox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also does Reach/Mana per spell have a limit? </div> </div> </div>Reach doesn't have a hard usage limit (though the dangers of Paradox are present), but Mana can only be spent on instant-cast spells as fast as your per-turn limit allows you to and you can't spend Mana you don't have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And permanent &amp; Until Dispelled are different I assume in that permanent can't be dispelled </div> </div> </div>Permanent would be in the vein of actually buying the new Trait dots with experience; spells mostly don't accomplish that on their own and so can be undone by other mages with a relatively simple spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T01:47:49-07:00","id":1082180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082167-augment-mind-limit-to-reach-mana-turn-and-spells-with-crossover-in-mind?p=1082175#post1082175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So for clarification of this as the storyteller of the game, (player was asking about it, as I wondered if he could just give the party ridiculous permanent bonuses as he thought it was unfair so I figured I'd check), what do you mean about the willpower investment? Also does Reach/Mana per spell have a limit? And permanent &amp; Until Dispelled are different I assume in that permanent can't be dispelled - sorry Mage compared to all the other splats does my head in , the rules seem so complicated even after reading it so many times xD.<br /> <br /> Also - Thanks for the help ^-^ in advance</div> </div> </div> </div>From all ive read it seems Mages and Demon are of similar power levels, the vampire however will probably be outclassed by them both compounded by only being able to work at night?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T01:51:33-07:00","id":1082183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082167-augment-mind-limit-to-reach-mana-turn-and-spells-with-crossover-in-mind?p=1082179#post1082179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making a spell not count towards your Gnosis limit of controlled spells without causing the effect to degrade over time requires that the caster spend a Willpower dot, which costs experience to repurchase. Until then, that spell counts toward your spell control and effectively reduces the number of spells you can have active at the same time by one until you end the spell, which makes it harder to cast other spells without risking Paradox.<br /> <br /> Reach doesn't have a hard usage limit (though the dangers of Paradox are present), but Mana can only be spent on instant-cast spells as fast as your per-turn limit allows you to and you can't spend Mana you don't have.<br /> <br /> Permanent would be in the vein of actually buying the new Trait dots with experience; spells mostly don't accomplish that on their own and so can be undone by other mages with a relatively simple spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>So your Gnosis limit of controlled spells - is it one for one? Example: Gnosis of 5 has a controlled spell limit of 5? Basically - the player was effectively saying could be using permenant spells be used to bypass and provide new traits with providing xp so if he was able to cast a spell like this at Gnosis 5 on a party member giving them like 3 intelligence for example. I appreciate the advice from you &amp; totalgit btw <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - this is clearing up much of my confusion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T02:08:37-07:00","id":1082189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082167-augment-mind-limit-to-reach-mana-turn-and-spells-with-crossover-in-mind?p=1082183#post1082183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So your Gnosis limit of controlled spells - is it one for one? Example: Gnosis of 5 has a controlled spell limit of 5? Basically - the player was effectively saying could be using permenant spells be used to bypass and provide new traits with providing xp so if he was able to cast a spell like this at Gnosis 5 on a party member giving them like 3 intelligence for example. I appreciate the advice from you &amp; totalgit btw <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - this is clearing up much of my confusion!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep 1 for 1. How much has the player read of 2e? Using terms like permanent spells etc one thinks he also hasnt got a good grasp of it yet ??<br /> <br /> So its fairly easy for a mage to give 5 people +3 Intelligence, its only +1 reach to advanced duration and then base targets are 5. It'd require the +2 reach if that +3 made any of the targets go over the limit tho. Mages are powerful, remember using mind 2 and some +2 reach and mana, a praxis spell to get 3 successes and avoid withstand and mages can mind control anything to commit suicide.<br /> <br /> Sounds like you and him really need to brush up on what his mage is capable off before allowing it? I wouldnt take his word on it from the sounds of it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T08:35:11-07:00","id":1082273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Volke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082167-augment-mind-limit-to-reach-mana-turn-and-spells-with-crossover-in-mind?p=1082183#post1082183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So your Gnosis limit of controlled spells - is it one for one? Example: Gnosis of 5 has a controlled spell limit of 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is indeed the standard progression. There's a couple of built-in workarounds, like Sanctums and Banner-Bearers, but both of those have requirements that potentially complicate things, either by needing you to be casting the spell within the Sanctum or needing you to have a sympathetic connection to the Sleepwalker that's stronger than what you'd get by just casting a spell on them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Basically - the player was effectively saying could be using permenant spells be used to bypass and provide new traits with providing xp so if he was able to cast a spell like this at Gnosis 5 on a party member giving them like 3 intelligence for example. </div> </div> </div>Most spells that are actually permanent are only permanent in that the consequences of reshaping/destroying part or all of a subject aren't undone when the spell ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T09:40:06-07:00","id":1082291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1082167-augment-mind-limit-to-reach-mana-turn-and-spells-with-crossover-in-mind?p=1082189#post1082189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep 1 for 1. How much has the player read of 2e? Using terms like permanent spells etc one thinks he also hasnt got a good grasp of it yet ??<br /> <br /> So its fairly easy for a mage to give 5 people +3 Intelligence, its only +1 reach to advanced duration and then base targets are 5. It'd require the +2 reach if that +3 made any of the targets go over the limit tho. Mages are powerful, remember using mind 2 and some +2 reach and mana, a praxis spell to get 3 successes and avoid withstand and mages can mind control anything to commit suicide.<br /> <br /> Sounds like you and him really need to brush up on what his mage is capable off before allowing it? I wouldnt take his word on it from the sounds of it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes - You are probably right, I need to brush up on it; just that I've been running a crossover game with like...all the major splats in so I've had to learn about like all of them :P . Anyways - Thanks for the help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11457-volke","name":"Volke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11457_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T09:32:48-07:00","id":1084523,"title":"","content":"Of course, the Vampire himself is considered a Sleepwalker for banner bearer and could carry the spell himself.<br /> <br /> As a practical matter, a starting mage with an Augment the Mind rote can grant + 3 Intelligence &amp; + 2 Resolve for 5 individuals Indefinitely.<br /> <br /> It would be Gnosis 1 + Mind 3 + 2 High Speech + 4 Rote Skill + 5 Ritual + 3 Willpower = 18 - 10 (Indefinite) - 4 (Extra Potency for Resolve) = 4 dice.<br /> <br /> It's a 15 hour ritual with a 75% chance of success.<br /> <br /> It requires +1 Reach to enhance two stats + 1 Reach for Indefinite + 1 Reach for Advanced Scale and +1 Reach for Advanced duration = 4 Reach<br /> <br /> This means the paradox pool will be 1 die. Fairly easily contained.<br /> <br /> Personally I would do it for 1 Year and include Wits for +2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 04-27-2017, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}